[pybind11] Free instance dict contents on Python 3.14

Backport of pybind/pybind11#5999 (fixes pybind/pybind11#5998), which is
released in pybind11 3.0.3. The 2.13.6 release that we use does not have it.

With Python 3.14, tp_free no longer clears the managed __dict__ of an
object, so the contents of the instance dict of a py::dynamic_attr()
object were never released when the object was destroyed by reference
counting (as opposed to by the garbage collector). Anything referred to
only from such a dict, e.g., the callbacks kept alive by pydrake's
ensure_callback_lifetime<>, leaked.

The upstream change also adds a unit test, which is omitted here.

Retire this patch when upgrading to pybind11 3.0.3 or newer.

--- include/pybind11/detail/class.h
+++ include/pybind11/detail/class.h
@@ -469,6 +469,17 @@
         PyObject_GC_UnTrack(self);
     }
 
+#if PY_VERSION_HEX >= 0x030D0000
+    // PyObject_ClearManagedDict() is available from Python 3.13+. It must be
+    // called before tp_free() because on Python 3.14+ tp_free no longer
+    // implicitly clears the managed dict, which would abandon the refcounts of
+    // objects stored in __dict__ of py::dynamic_attr() types, causing permanent
+    // memory leaks.
+    if (PyType_HasFeature(type, Py_TPFLAGS_MANAGED_DICT)) {
+        PyObject_ClearManagedDict(self);
+    }
+#endif
+
     clear_instance(self);
 
     type->tp_free(self);
